## What Problem This Solves

Fixes an issue where `/thinking high|low|medium` was rejected with "not supported for github-copilot/claude-sonnet-4.6, use one of: off" for dynamically-discovered Copilot Claude models, even though the backing Claude model supports reasoning. Only `off` was advertised.

## Why This Change Was Made

Copilot's `/models` endpoint does not expose OpenAI-style `reasoning_effort` for Anthropic-backed models, so model discovery marks every Copilot-discovered Claude model `reasoning: false`. The shared thinking resolver (`src/auto-reply/thinking.ts`) then discarded github-copilot's declared level set and fell back to off-only, because neither thinking surface set `preserveWhenCatalogReasoningFalse`. This PR sets that flag for Claude models (detected via the existing `anthropic-messages` transport signal) on BOTH github-copilot thinking surfaces, mirroring `anthropic`, `amazon-bedrock`, `google`, and `moonshot`:
- the active provider hook (`resolveThinkingProfile` in `index.ts`), and
- the bundled provider-policy surface (`provider-policy-api.ts`, used by `/think`, ACP controls, and directive parsing when no active plugin supplies the hook).

This preserves the levels the hooks already declare (`off/minimal/low/medium/high`) and invents no new ones; non-Claude Copilot models without `reasoning_effort` stay off-only.

Per review on #99240: both thinking surfaces must agree before merge.

## User Impact

Users running Copilot-routed Claude models (e.g. `claude-sonnet-4.6`, `claude-opus-4.7`) can use `/thinking high|low|medium` as expected, instead of being locked to `off` — across the active provider path and the bundled/directive path.

## Evidence

- `extensions/github-copilot/index.test.ts`: a Claude model resolves `preserveWhenCatalogReasoningFalse: true` with the `[off,minimal,low,medium,high]` level set; a non-Claude model (`gpt-5.4-mini`) leaves the flag unset.
- `extensions/github-copilot/provider-policy-api.test.ts`: the same assertions for the bundled policy surface (Claude → flag set; non-Claude → unset) — 11/11 pass.
- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.extension-providers.config.ts extensions/github-copilot`: thinking tests pass. The full github-copilot suite only has pre-existing Windows `EBUSY` SQLite-teardown flakes in token-onboarding tests, unrelated to this change.

Live end-to-end Copilot proof (a real `/thinking high` round-trip) still requires a maintainer with Copilot credentials; the code fix is complete on both surfaces and covered by the unit tests above.

## Standalone harness proof (outside the test runner)

ClawSweeper flagged unit-test-only evidence. The transcript below is produced by a **standalone harness** (`npx tsx`, **no** vitest, **no** mocks, **no** `expect`) that drives the **real shared thinking resolver** (`src/auto-reply/thinking.ts` — the exact user-facing path that decides which `/thinking` levels a model offers) plus the **real Copilot provider-policy** (`provider-policy-api.ts`, the code this PR changes). It feeds the catalog shape live discovery produces for Copilot Anthropic-backed models (`reasoning: false`).

**Layer 2 is the merge-relevant result:** it shows the full resolver path. Under `catalog reasoning: false`, `github-copilot/claude-sonnet-4.6` now offers `[off,minimal,low,medium,high]` (so `/thinking high` is accepted — fixing #99240), while the non-Claude `gpt-5.4-mini` still collapses to `[off]`.

```
=== Copilot thinking standalone harness ===
(real shared resolver + real Copilot provider-policy; no vitest, no mocks)

--- Layer 1: Copilot provider-policy emission (the code this PR changes) ---
  claude-sonnet-4.6: preserveWhenCatalogReasoningFalse=true  declared levels=[off,minimal,low,medium,high]
  gpt-5.4-mini: preserveWhenCatalogReasoningFalse=<unset>  declared levels=[off,minimal,low,medium,high]
  -> Claude opts in to preserve; non-Claude does not.

--- Layer 2: shared resolver end-to-end (catalog reasoning:false -> offered /thinking levels) ---
  github-copilot/claude-sonnet-4.6 (catalog reasoning:false):
    offered /thinking levels = [off,minimal,low,medium,high]  -> PRESERVED
    expected: preserved (off..high)

  github-copilot/gpt-5.4-mini (catalog reasoning:false):
    offered /thinking levels = [off]  -> OFF-ONLY (high rejected)
    expected: collapsed (off-only)

--- Conclusion ---
  Copilot Claude (claude-sonnet-4.6) under catalog reasoning:false now offers
  [off,minimal,low,medium,high] -> /thinking high is accepted (fixes #99240).
  Non-Claude Copilot (gpt-5.4-mini) without the preserve flag still collapses
  to off-only, so reasoning is not advertised to models that may not support it.
```

The non-Claude `gpt-5.4-mini` row is the control for the pre-fix behavior: any Copilot model without `preserveWhenCatalogReasoningFalse` collapses to off-only under `reasoning: false` — exactly what happened to Claude on main. The PR's only effect is opting Claude into the existing preserve path; it adds no new levels.

This exercises the complete in-repo code path (catalog → shared resolver → offered levels). The remaining unprovable step is the Copilot API accepting the `/thinking high` request at the wire level, which needs Copilot credentials the contributor does not have.

> Note on the ClawSweeper "stored data model" flag: thinking profiles are runtime-resolved from provider policy + catalog metadata and are not persisted, embedded, or migrated — there is no data-model or vector/embedding change in this diff.

<details>
<summary>Harness source — reproducible; save as <code>proof-copilot-thinking.ts</code> at the repo root and run <code>npx tsx proof-copilot-thinking.ts</code></summary>

```ts
// Standalone Copilot thinking harness — NOT a vitest test.
//
// Drives the REAL shared thinking resolver (src/auto-reply/thinking.ts), which
// is the exact user-facing path that decides which /thinking levels a model
// offers, plus the REAL Copilot provider-policy (provider-policy-api.ts) the PR
// changes. No vitest, no mocks, no expect. Prints a transcript showing that a
// Copilot Claude model keeps off..high under catalog reasoning:false (so
// /thinking high is offered, fixing #99240), while a non-Claude Copilot model
// still collapses to off-only.
//
// Run:  npx tsx proof-copilot-thinking.ts
import { resolveThinkingProfile as resolveShared } from "./src/auto-reply/thinking.js";
import { resolveThinkingProfile as resolveCopilotPolicy } from "./extensions/github-copilot/provider-policy-api.js";

type AnyRecord = Record<string, unknown>;
const ll = (p: AnyRecord | null | undefined) =>
  (p?.levels as { id: string }[] | undefined)?.map((l) => l.id) ?? [];

// Copilot /models does not advertise OpenAI reasoning_effort for Anthropic-backed
// models, so live discovery marks them reasoning:false — this is the catalog row
// shape that triggered the off-only collapse on main.
function copilotCatalogEntry(id: string) {
  return { provider: "github-copilot", id, reasoning: false } as AnyRecord;
}

console.log("=== Copilot thinking standalone harness ===");
console.log("(real shared resolver + real Copilot provider-policy; no vitest, no mocks)\n");

console.log("--- Layer 1: Copilot provider-policy emission (the code this PR changes) ---");
for (const modelId of ["claude-sonnet-4.6", "gpt-5.4-mini"]) {
  const profile = resolveCopilotPolicy({
    provider: "github-copilot",
    modelId,
    compat: { supportedReasoningEfforts: [] },
  }) as AnyRecord;
  const preserve = profile?.preserveWhenCatalogReasoningFalse;
  console.log(
    `  ${modelId}: preserveWhenCatalogReasoningFalse=${preserve === true ? "true" : "<unset>"}  declared levels=[${ll(profile).join(",")}]`,
  );
}
console.log("  -> Claude opts in to preserve; non-Claude does not.\n");

console.log("--- Layer 2: shared resolver end-to-end (catalog reasoning:false -> offered /thinking levels) ---");
const cases: { model: string; expect: string }[] = [
  { model: "claude-sonnet-4.6", expect: "preserved (off..high)" },
  { model: "gpt-5.4-mini", expect: "collapsed (off-only)" },
];
for (const c of cases) {
  const profile = resolveShared({
    provider: "github-copilot",
    model: c.model,
    catalog: [copilotCatalogEntry(c.model)],
  }) as AnyRecord;
  const levels = ll(profile);
  const isOffOnly = levels.length === 1 && levels[0] === "off";
  console.log(
    `  github-copilot/${c.model} (catalog reasoning:false):`,
  );
  console.log(`    offered /thinking levels = [${levels.join(",")}]  -> ${isOffOnly ? "OFF-ONLY (high rejected)" : "PRESERVED"}`);
  console.log(`    expected: ${c.expect}\n`);
}

console.log("--- Conclusion ---");
console.log("  Copilot Claude (claude-sonnet-4.6) under catalog reasoning:false now offers");
console.log("  [off,minimal,low,medium,high] -> /thinking high is accepted (fixes #99240).");
console.log("  Non-Claude Copilot (gpt-5.4-mini) without the preserve flag still collapses");
console.log("  to off-only, so reasoning is not advertised to models that may not support it.");
```

